  "scope": "One disposable Kubernetes v1.36.1 Kind cluster runs three native, short-lived Jobs using a digest-pinned Python image. Each Job reads only checked-in synthetic metadata: an inert dataset string, a training-run record marked not performed, and a metadata-only model artifact placeholder. The Jobs check schema/task identifiers, fixture digests, scope labels, and release-to-run artifact references. Separate Job status and logs expose a consistent development fixture, a deliberate release provenance mismatch, and an out-of-profile operation record whose governance and actual operation remain unknown. This does not train or load a model, establish organizational compliance, evaluate real data or weights, prove production provenance, or assess deployment/operation controls. Separate local Jobs gate a synthetic feature on the exact manifest and partition bytes, and a read-only Job checks the expected output or its absence. Two case-owned namespaces compare bounded Kubernetes API authorization with short-lived projected ServiceAccount identities. A temporary cross-namespace binding establishes successful GET and LIST; its removal denies those requests for the developer while own reads and approved protected reads remain allowed. The readbacks follow the same immutable objects and the exact Job-owned Pods. Adopter evidence covers the broader PO.5.1 practice.",
